{
  "variants": [
    {
      "persona": "Whitehat Hacker",
      "taskMessage": "<b>Dr. Mira Sen:</b> You kept the scan inside the signed range. Good. Scope discipline does not make the work smaller, it makes the evidence usable. Now the approved network gets its turn to tell us what does not belong in it.",
      "taskInstructions": "",
      "taskQuestion": "",
      "taskCompleteText": "<b>Dr. Mira Sen:</b> Compare the scan with the expected inventory and document only what the evidence supports."
    },
    {
      "persona": "Blackhat Hacker",
      "taskMessage": "<b>Kade Mercer:</b> Private notes are only worth something if they show what the official map missed. Quiet work first, inside the range nobody will question, and the asset the paperwork never named is where this gets interesting.",
      "taskInstructions": "",
      "taskQuestion": "",
      "taskCompleteText": "<b>Kade Mercer:</b> Show me the response the official inventory cannot explain."
    },
    {
      "persona": "Hacktivist",
      "taskMessage": "<b>Lena Ortiz:</b> Public pressure only works when the proof is clean. The camera question can wait another hour; right now the approved range has to answer for itself, and it has to do that without creating a new risk we would end up explaining to riders.",
      "taskInstructions": "",
      "taskQuestion": "",
      "taskCompleteText": "<b>Lena Ortiz:</b> Keep the finding clean enough that the city cannot dismiss it."
    }
  ],
  "taskID": "ismg6860_u02_q04_t00_dialogue",
